A||||9||BlackStang95||HID headlight upgrade replacement (general)||||5||
Z||000000||BlackStang95||10-11-2001||09:46 PM||||What all is involved in upgrading to HID headlights...can you do it yourself...what's it cost...etc.? ||||reg||5
Z||000001||Mach10||10-11-2001||10:02 PM||||HooF! That's a can o'worms! I think there was one member that did it, though... Can't remember who. Try a search...<P>Problems involve: <BR>-Different "bulb" design<BR>-Insane heat ouput<BR>-Finding one the right size/shape<BR>||||reg||10
Z||000002||gt boy||10-11-2001||10:28 PM||||from what i understand...you have to do a complete rewire so the system can handle the power draw.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||snafus87||10-11-2001||11:06 PM||||from what I've read, the HID lighting system actually uses less power than standard incandescent lighting OR halogen lighting...BUT I could be wrong...just think I remember reading that somewhere.<P>------------------<BR>JT Krupa<BR>85 GT<BR>(fastback conversion)<BR>180+ K miles<BR>Lehighton, PA||||reg||1
Z||000004||Bigfieroman||10-12-2001||01:46 AM||||They are also illegal (I think) in 50 states.  They are only legal if the car was made with them.<P>------------------<BR>87 GT Automatic, Beretta GTZ Wheels, Kuhmo Ecsta Supra 712 tires, Poly cradle bushings.<BR>Future mods: Complete suspension redux w/anti-bumpsteer, all poly, rear swaybar, KYBs, Ground Control Coilovers, Street Dreams lowering spindles, plus exterior redux, w/window and quater panel scoops, Kid Danger air dam, 1fst2m6 style hood vent, IRM Whale Tail Spioler, and black w/ silver racing stripes paint.<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigpic_5.JPG">    <P>3800 S/C after all that!||||reg||1
Z||000005||Htown86GT||10-12-2001||09:08 AM||||There are now companies that make HID lights in all bulb configurations, ie H4, H1, H7.<BR>The kit usually costs anywhere from $400 to $600 - <BR> <A HREF="http://www.lltek.com/about_HID.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.lltek.com/about_HID.htm</A> <P>that is the Kit for A4/S$ which I will be purchasing.  <P>You can use these on Fieros but you will need a Headlamp with a beam pattern that points at the ground (Projection Beam) because the light is so bright that it will <BR>blind oncoming traffic.<P>  <IMG SRC="http://home.swbell.net/ravi1/myauditswair.jpg">  <P> <IMG SRC="http://home.swbell.net/ravi1/myfiero.jpg"> <p>[This message has been edited by Htown86GT (edited 10-12-2001).]||||reg||3
Z||000006||MinnGreenGT||10-12-2001||09:31 AM||||I found an online store a couple of days ago... <A HREF="http://www.xtremewhite.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.xtremewhite.com</A>  who offers a HID upgrade kit for H4 and some others.  For a fiero (or similiar std. system) you'll need to initially replace the stock bulb assembly with one that accepts the H4 bulb system (available through the FieroStore and easily found on Ebay).  XtremeWhite then offers (for $600) an upgrade kit.  Keep in mind that replacement bulbs are $140ea!||||reg||1
Z||000007||Htown86GT||10-12-2001||10:11 AM||||There is also a newer HID bulb that phillips makes now that gives that purplish HID light output.  Its puts out light output at 6000k as opposed to the regular HID which has an output of 4500k.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000008||Adrift||10-12-2001||12:15 PM||||There is a guy on ebay who sells kits for $40 bucks - anyone know of anything wrong with them?<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000009||MinnGreenGT||10-12-2001||12:28 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Adrift:<BR><B>There is a guy on ebay who sells kits for $40 bucks - anyone know of anything wrong with them?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>The $40 kit is not really a HID upgrade.  Just allows you to use a H4 style bulb. I've got that style kit on my Car... nice & I think worth the $40.  But still not HID.  Check with Artherd- he did the HID upgrade himself.||||reg||1
